  "mathematics": [
    "Two adjacent whole positive components would have respective actual negative neighbors with the same left/right root. Closed negative index uniqueness forces those neighbors equal, contradicting their positive length. This reuses the existing actual simple-root neighbor theorem.",
    "A negative half whose interface is its middle cut cannot occur at a profile root, because that cut lies in its strictly negative component.",
    "Two negative outer halves meeting at the root are excluded by the same actual closed negative index uniqueness.",
    "The remaining ordered cases are exactly negative(m,true) followed by positive p with positiveLeft p=right(m), and positive p followed by negative(m,false) with positiveRight p=left(m).",
    "Actual reference radii and unchanged new-gauge physical metadata transfer the complete classification to the same e-indexed atlas. No root first-jet matching assumption is used."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
